 "note": "Olive: the owner's own orange mackerel tabby (no white socks): darker ginger stripes, ringed tail with a darker tip, tabby M, pale cream belly / inner thighs / chin / muzzle, pink nose, pink inner ears, yellow-green eyes with a lazy eye (both pupils on the outer edges), olive-green collar with a glowing green olive charm (red pimento). Egg-only, never spawns naturally.",
 "ability_desc": "Purr Therapy: when you're hurt he trots over, flops belly-up right next to you with his paws curled and purrs, and you get Regeneration while he does. A soft, slightly round orange mackerel tabby: darker ginger stripes down his sides, a ringed tail with a darker tip, the tabby M on his forehead, a pale cream belly and chin, a pink nose and yellow-green eyes with a lazy eye (both pupils point outward, which gives him his sweet derpy stare). He wears an olive-green collar with a little glowing green olive charm. 83 clips, 25 of his own: lies belly-up on bath mats (carpets) staring up at you, loafs and stares like he's sitting in the bathtub, does the derpy stare with his tongue out, mlems, wobbles his wall-eyed head, tilts his head at noises, kneads, wriggle-rolls on his back, chases his tail until he falls over, sploots, washes, stretches, gets the zoomies and flops, and pays for fish by showing you his belly. Greets you with a bouncy trot, two head-bonks and a flop, and does puffed-up sideways hops at creepers. Petting: head rubs, belly rolls and slow love blinks; pet him too much and his belly turns into a trap: he grabs your hand with all four paws and bunny-kicks it. Not found in the wild: spawn him with his egg; he arrives already named Olive and is tamed with raw cod.",
